WEBVTT

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.620
I'm home, honey! Your father has returned!

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.450
Welcome home, Mamoru-<i>sama</i>.
So where is Maeve-<i>sama</i>?

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.580
Maeve said she had some loose ends to tie up.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.040
She will be back after
stopping by her family's home.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.580
Aw, man...

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.870
I wanted to come back home together, myself.
Don't put the blame on me.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.950
It sounds like you did well, Makoto-<i>kun</i>.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.160
Oh, no, not really.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.580
It was really lucky for me that you came along.
You have my cordial welcome.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.200
Thank you very much.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.330
I will work hard to become a magician
who is on par with you, Master.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:51.200
Hmm, there is nothing more for me to teach you.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.540
Huh?

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.120
I can't do the kind of magic
you're talking about.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.580
All of my magic is accomplished by
means of the power of Maeve's Artifact.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.500
They say if you want to hide a tree,
put it in the forest, right?

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.250
With me as the magician,
it doesn't draw attention toward Maeve.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:32.500
<i>Tell me, do you remember?</i>

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.410
<i>Yes, the wondrous God-given power you have,</i>

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:42.250
<i>like sleight of hand without any tricks?</i>

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.040
<i>Tell me, have you already forgotten?</i>

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.200
<i>Those dreamlike, heart-shaped</i>

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.620
<i>flower-bouquet-like words of yours?</i>

00:01:54.620 --> 00:02:00.870
<i>I'm sure, I'm sure</i>

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:04.500
<i>this key will open your treasure box</i>

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.750
<i>and let you remember them tonight</i>

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.620
<i>Farewell!</i>

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:14.910
<i>Watch me now,</i>

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.120
<i>I'm gently, quietly going to disappear,</i>

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.040
<i>so find me</i>

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.250
<i>I'm over here</i>

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.370
<i>Our long, long night of secrets is beginning</i>

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.660
<i>Come after me</i>

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.830
<i>Once you see the twinkle of my tearstains,</i>

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.750
<i>catch me with your voice</i>

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.450
<i>and the magic words only the two of us know</i>

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.700
On the other hand, Mamoru-<i>kun</i>,
just being able to use an Artifact

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.250
does not make you a first-rate magician.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.870
There's also command of the stage,
speaking persuasively, appearance,

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.120
and many other things that you should learn.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.040
R-Right.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.370
Okay, time to apply yourself.
I have to go overseas again though.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.950
Adieu!

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.540
Big brother, how's this?

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.000
Yeah, sure. The trick is
to direct their attention

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.040
away from the hand that is holding the candy.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.410
Mm-hm, I'll try.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.750
H-Hatena? What is it?

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.040
You sure seem to be enjoying yourselves.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.450
W-Well, um, yeah. Yumemi-<i>chan </i>asked me to, so...

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.870
Somehow, I'm not convinced.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.830
I'm Miss Nagase, Yumemi-<i>chan</i>'s homeroom teacher.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.330
I'm sorry to always have to be calling on you.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.080
Not at all.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.200
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>!

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.620
You're looking well.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.580
Yumemi!

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.660
I'm sorry. I'll go get her right now.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:07.410
Oh, that's okay. It isn't right to force her.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:11.910
These are the worksheets from
the time she's missed and a letter.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.870
I'm sorry about this.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.750
Yumemi, why did you run away today?

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.660
Your teacher and friend came
all the way here, just for you.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.080
I don't think that's very nice.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.910
Why aren't you going to school?
Did one of your friends do something to you?

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.620
You can't just stay home
from school forever, you know.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.410
Would you talk to me?
Maybe we can figure this out.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.290
It isn't any of your business.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.290
Well, of course it's my business!

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.290
Hatena, if you yell at Yumemi-<i>chan </i>like that,

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:51.500
she may not be able to
tell you what she wants to.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:55.410
But Yumemi hasn't been to
school in over a week now!

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.200
Huh? Is that right?

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:02.660
Tell me, Yumemi, why aren't you going
to school? At least tell me the reason!

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.000
No.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.700
Wh-Why not?

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.870
I want you to just leave me alone.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.160
Hold it, Yumemi!

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.500
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>...

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.580
I wonder if I've gotten on Yumemi's bad side.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:24.580
Oh, yeah? The dolly is still having trouble?

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:30.120
She seems so soft and gentle,
with stunningly brilliant and pretty looks!

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:36.200
Yumemi-<i>chan </i>is the ultimate doll-like beauty,
sent by God to our world!

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:41.250
This is why Yumemi always avoids you, Kokomi.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.700
She can't take you
because you lack any delicacy.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:47.660
It's that crisp, dry nature of hers
that makes her so charming.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.580
I've got it! After class,
let's go over to Yumemi's school.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.160
Why would we do that?

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.750
To find out the reason why
Yumemi-<i>chan </i>has quit going to school.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.540
Yeah, but what good is our
sudden arrival going to do?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.620
Not to worry. Do you just want
to let things go on like this?

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.160
Well, no...

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.330
You're coming, too! You're a member
of the Hoshisato family at this point!

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.250
M-Mm-hmm...

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:13.580
Wait up!

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.790
Excuse us!

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.830
Wow, they're giving us super-weird looks.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:27.080
Well, some people in middle-school
uniforms just showed up at their door.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.250
Hold your heads high. We're doing
this for Yumemi-<i>chan</i>, remember?

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.830
Out of my way! Let me through!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.540
Hey, you! What do you think
you're doing to my Hatena?!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:45.000
Let me go! It's your own fault
for spacing out in the doorway!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.500
Take that!

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.250
Heh! Those are cute panties for
such a good-for-nothing old biddy!

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.330
You stinking little brat!

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:59.540
Hatena, I've figured it out. Yumemi-<i>chan </i>has
been bullied by that vulgar monster,

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.080
right here in this class!

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:05.410
E-Excuse me, you're Yumemi-<i>chan</i>'s
sister and brother, right?

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.450
Oh, you're that girl who came over.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.870
How is Yumemi-<i>chan </i>doing?

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.750
Oh, she's fine.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:15.450
She is? Thank goodness.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.790
Mami-<i>chan</i>, is it? Would you tell us something?

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.910
Yes.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.660
Is the reason Yumemi-<i>chan</i>
stopped coming to school

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:25.790
because the boys are picking on her?

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:28.370
I don't think that's why.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:33.370
Yumemi-<i>chan </i>never seemed to be
bothered when the boys were mean.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:36.700
Then is there anything else you can think of?

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.330
Hmm, then again, not long ago,

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:42.250
when one of the boys broke
a bear that she made of clay,

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.040
she seemed a bit upset.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:48.250
So that's what happened.
Did they end up fighting, or anything?

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:52.580
No, Yumemi-<i>chan </i>made it over again right away.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.660
It turned out even better than before,

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:58.080
and she got a commendation from the principal!

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.620
Thanks for telling us.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:04.290
If you like, we'd appreciate it if
you came to visit Yumemi-<i>chan </i>again.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.410
Sure! I'd love that, too!

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.000
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>?

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:16.040
Y-Yumemi? I'm sorry about earlier.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.330
What are you doing here, big sister?

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.620
I only want to talk to Makoto-<i>niisama</i>.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:24.830
O-Oh, don't be like that.
Have some tea with me, okay?

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:27.580
That's okay. I already have some sweets.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:31.660
Makoto-<i>niisama</i>, teach me some more magic later.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.370
M-Mm-hmm, okay, sure.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.950
Why will she only talk to you?

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.660
You went to her <i>school</i>?

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:42.910
Yes.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:47.370
With all of the meddling going
on in Mistress Yumemi's life,

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:50.540
I wish she would finally resume her studies.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:55.160
Well, Kikyouin-<i>san </i>insisted today,
or at least that's how it seemed.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:00.040
The madam asking us to be extra
watchful must have been a great factor.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.790
You mean Maeve-<i>san</i>?

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:06.620
The madam may have anticipated
things ending up like this.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:10.700
I can do little more than
carefully watch over her,

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:17.250
but <i>you</i>, on the other hand...
Take good care of those two, will you?

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.620
Right.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.910
It's Mami-<i>chan</i>.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.870
You came right away, I see.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:28.410
Huh? But if you've already
been shown inside, then...

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:32.200
Mistress Yumemi will see
you in the reception room.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.450
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>, I'm so glad to see you today.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:40.290
Did you read the letter I wrote you?

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.080
Mm-hmm, I did.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:48.290
We have a funfest coming up.
You and I will be in the same group again.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.910
Oh, yeah?

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:53.830
Ah, but Ryusei-<i>kun </i>will be in our group, too.

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:57.540
That boy is always picking on you, huh?

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:58.700
Does he?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:03.120
Yumemi, you have to do more talking.
She came all the way here for you.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.000
I think it's time I stepped in and...

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.790
Hatena, take it easy.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.200
Wait, Hatena!

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.410
Ow...

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.120
Big sister, Makoto-<i>niisama</i>, what are you doing?

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:19.120
Oh, um, I was just cleaning, and slipped...

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.950
I'm sorry, but we were just so concerned.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:28.000
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>'s sister, I apologize
for what that boy in our class did to you.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.080
Mami-<i>chan</i>, what do you mean?

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:34.790
Oh, you know what?
They were worried about you earlier,

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:37.000
so they came over to our school.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.660
Big sister, you went to my class?

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:43.080
Yeah, just to ask what was going on.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.250
Why would you do that?

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.750
Yumemi, what's wrong?

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:48.580
Idiot!

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.700
I hate you!

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.370
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>!

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:55.540
Um... Um...

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.450
I'm sorry about that. It's all right.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:04.330
Good morning, Yumemi-<i>chan</i>.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.250
Big brother, are you alone?

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:10.700
Mm-hmm, it's just me.
Hatena is feeling awfully down.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.450
Do you really hate her now?

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:19.370
No, I don't. I'm just a little upset.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:24.250
Hatena is really concerned about you.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.540
I know that.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:30.330
What should I do?

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.830
I have just the thing for you, Yumemi-<i>chan</i>.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:40.790
Big brother, that's amazing.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:44.410
I think magic is a fast-acting cure for tears.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:49.330
I, too, was once helped out
by Master Mamoru's magic.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.540
You're even better than Father.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:56.870
Th-That's not true at all.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.120
Big sister...

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.660
Yumemi?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:06.160
Big sister, I'm sorry I said
I hate you yesterday.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:11.120
Yumemi! Mm-mm, it's okay.
I'm sorry I butted in, too.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:14.200
I mean, sure, if I had mean boys
like that at my school,

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:17.540
I wouldn't want to go, either.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:21.160
Hmm? I'm not really getting picked on.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:26.450
Huh? The reason you don't want to go
to school isn't because of those brats?

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:28.160
Mm-mm, it's not.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.830
Then why aren't you going to school?

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.830
I just don't want to go.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.000
Wait, hold on a second.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.500
In that case, get yourself to school.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.790
No.

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:41.790
Don't "no" me!

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:45.250
You have to go to school, or you won't
grow up to be someone respectable.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:48.330
The lessons at school are too easy.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:53.200
That's not the issue!
Either way, you still have to go to school!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.040
No.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.200
Yumemi!

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:58.500
If that's how you want it,
I'll force you to go back to school!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.080
Muff-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:05.410
H-Hold on, Hatena! You can't
use that against Yumemi-<i>chan</i>!

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.370
Makoto-<i>sama</i>, no!

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:11.290
It is my humble opinion

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.080
that we are the ones who are in greater danger.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.700
Gaugau!

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:25.250
That is Yumemi-<i>sama</i>'s own private Artifact.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:29.160
When Gaugau is summoned to guard Yumemi-<i>sama</i>,

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:34.080
he is an all-powerful stuffed animal,
with many kinds of magic within.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.870
Yumemi, no matter what,
I'm taking you back to school!

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.870
Go, Muff-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.410
Muff-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.700
Ah, Muff-<i>kun</i>!

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:12.700
Mistress Kana has gotten even better.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.450
If you are comparing the two,
I am expecting Mistress Yumemi

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:19.000
to perform one of her legendary
pro-gamer dramatic reversals of fortune.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.000
Is now the time for you to be
giving casual color commentary?!

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.250
Not to worry.
Both of their Artifacts are designed

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:28.750
to give the safety of their
contract bearers top priority.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:32.330
On top of which, the mansion
can use its Artifact power

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:36.660
to automatically repair some degree of damage.

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:56.120
H-Hold on, both of you!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:57.370
Makoto-<i>sama</i>?!

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.540
Big brother?!

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.500
M-Makoto!

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.200
Ow...

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.410
How could you jump into the middle of that?

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:16.330
You're right. My legs just
kind of acted on their own.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.620
Makoto-<i>sama</i>?

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.870
I'm going up to Yumemi-<i>chan</i>'s room.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:23.870
I need to reassure her that I'm all right.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:29.410
Big brother, I really am sorry about today.

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:37.160
Ha, ha, it's perfectly all right. But you
did a real number on the entranceway.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:41.370
It's big sister's fault
for being such a hothead.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:45.700
She can't help but be concerned
about your school situation.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:49.700
I'm not going to school. I don't have to go.

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:54.450
Even if you're at too high a level
for the lessons to do you any good,

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:58.080
there are also other fun things
about school, aren't there?

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.120
The boys are annoying.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.120
That's a tricky problem to deal with.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:06.040
We don't look alike.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.410
Who doesn't look alike?

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:10.790
They say big sister and me don't look alike.

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:13.700
They say my blond hair is strange.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:17.250
Is that the reason you don't go to school?

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:20.200
Because the boys tease you about that?

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.120
Not exactly.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:28.370
It's common for sisters to have
different hair colors. I get that.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:32.410
But I don't like being told we're not alike.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.290
It's like a stabbing pain in my heart.

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:39.500
Yeah, sure. It hurts being
told you're different, doesn't it?

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:43.410
After all, you love your big sister, don't you?

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:54.750
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>, do you want to try
some magic tricks with cards today?

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.450
Really?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.950
Okay now, watch closely.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.660
Well?

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.870
So you know what?
Yumemi just stays up in her room,

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.870
sends Gaugau to do whatever she needs done,

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.790
and won't even show her face!

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.080
Are you listening to me, Kokomi?!

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:20.620
Yeah, yeah, I heard you. But how many
times are we going to talk about this?

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:25.040
Well, what else can I do?
We aren't making any progress.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:27.540
Why don't you force her out of her room?

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:31.660
I think you could pull that off if you took
Makoto-<i>kun </i>hostage or something.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.330
Hostage?

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:37.000
Silence! You presumed to
go inside the dolly's room!

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.620
Being taken hostage is
an appropriate punishment!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:43.870
Doing that isn't any good.
It doesn't solve anything.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.910
It's just a joke, silly.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:51.950
She once used to sit in my lap,
and I would brush her hair.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.790
But lately, Makoto, you've
taken all of that away from me.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:58.950
Aw, that silky blond hair of hers...

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:03.040
It's so much like Mama's, and
I used to be so happy just to touch it.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:07.580
What's this? Hatena, are you
jealous of Yumemi-<i>chan</i>?

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:11.830
Well, Yumemi takes after
Mama so much, and she's smart, too.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:15.160
If she went to school,
and studied what she's supposed to,

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:17.620
she could be just like Mama in the future--

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:21.370
mm-mm, she could be even greater than Mama.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.370
So I just think it's a shame.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:28.160
Hatena, I think your hair is pretty, too.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:31.620
The color of your hair doesn't matter.
You and Yumemi-<i>chan</i>...

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:36.290
...are sure to be different types
of beautiful women when you grow up.

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:39.290
Wh-Wh-What are you saying, Makoto?!

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:42.120
Huh? Did I say something out of place?

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:46.620
Nagase-<i>sensei </i>and friends are here.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:57.700
The boys said they wanted to come here
today to apologize to Yumemi-<i>chan</i>.

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:03.620
I'm sorry I smashed your clay bear
because I thought it was gross.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:07.450
I'm sorry for flipping your skirt up so much.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:11.120
I'm sorry for saying your hair was weird.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:20.620
L-Listen, your hair really isn't weird.
I think the gold color is pretty.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:28.250
Yumemi, they all apologized,
so now you should say something.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.830
Yumemi!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.290
Wait, Hatena. I'll go.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.290
Yumemi-<i>chan</i>?

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:42.250
I don't think that went very well back there.

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:45.700
I know you're sensitive about your hair.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:51.950
Hatena was standing right next to you, too.
But those boys don't know that.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:57.410
They just really think that
your hair is pretty, that's all.

00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:59.250
I don't get it.

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:04.700
I don't know how to answer
when someone tells me they're sorry.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:10.830
Hmm, okay. "That's all right"
or "you're forgiven," maybe?

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:16.410
All right, how about this, then?

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.620
Yumemi-<i>chan </i>says that there's
something she'd like to show you.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.290
Um...

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.580
Yumemi...

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.580
Not bad!

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.830
Everyone, put your hands into your pockets.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.790
Awesome!

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.500
How did you do that?!

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:56.540
Are the Hoshisatos really able to do magic?

00:20:56.540 --> 00:21:01.790
Mm-mm, no, it's just a trick.
There's a secret to it and everything.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.620
Even so, that was awesome!

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:06.450
Do it again! Let us see it again!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.370
--So awesome!
--What's going on here?!

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:13.790
--Awesome is right!
--Hey, show us how you do it sometime!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.950
Huh? What's wrong, Hatena?

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:19.660
Why do you get to steal
the whole show? It's not fair.

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:22.450
It's unfair and dirty, you big sneak!

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:32.700
Why, Tominozawa-<i>sama</i>...

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:36.830
Oh, Jeeves-<i>san</i>, please don't
call me by that formal name.

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:39.500
I'd like you to refer to me as "Tomi-Tomi."

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:42.080
What can we do for you today?

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:44.580
I was just in the neighborhood,

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:47.540
and I thought I would drop in and
say hello to Mamoru-<i>san </i>and Maeve-<i>san</i>.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:51.450
Unfortunately, neither the master
nor madam are at home right now.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:56.450
So it would seem. All right,
I shall come back some other day.

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:58.660
Have a nice day.

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:08.200
<i>My path now begins</i>

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:16.580
<i>I've unleashed the hidden light of one future</i>

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:22.950
<i>I've been on the hunt</i>

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:27.000
<i>to find my furthest dreams</i>

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:30.160
<i>I want to shine even brighter</i>

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:35.250
<i>The "someday" that my former self prayed for</i>

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:40.410
<i>is still far away, but I'll catch up</i>

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:45.450
<i>"Miracle" is such an embarrassingly vague word</i>

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:50.620
<i>My timeframe has neither forever nor a moment</i>

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:57.870
<i>I move forward one step at a time to my voice</i>

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:01.660
<i>No matter what awaits me</i>

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:03.000
<i>beyond this pain</i>

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.250
<i>I'll once again, yes once again</i>

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:08.000
<i>leap up and shine</i>

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:11.830
<i>Yeah, I'll put into words</i>

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:13.370
<i>the view laid out before me</i>

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:16.620
<i>and let it ring out dozens,</i>

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:20.290
<i>even hundreds of times</i>

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:24.580
<i>What color do you suppose love is?</i>

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:30.290
<i>I've unleashed my hidden light</i>

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:38.330
"What have you gotten mad about recently?"

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:51.910
"Tominozawa"

00:23:51.910 --> 00:24:01.830
"See you next time"
